Subject: [PATCH 0082] framebuffer: set IOFBDependentID so IOGraphics creates the framebuffer's controller

Wildcat Lake test 25: panic in IOFramebuffer::powerStateWillChangeTo (NULL+0x120, state 1, kIOPMDeviceUsable) right
after NMXGPU's framebuffer registered its power driver. IOFramebuffer::start takes the framebuffer's IOFBController
from IOFBController::copyController, which returns NULL unless the framebuffer has an IOFBDependentID (OSNumber)
property; every IOGraphics path that takes the controller's gate then reads NULL->+0x120 (also test 24's
IOFramebuffer::terminate). Set IOFBDependentID (the GPU's PCI registry ID) and IOFBDependentIndex 0 before
IOFramebuffer::start, as the GPU framebuffer drivers do.

diff --git a/gpu-port/xkpi/xnu/nmx_fb.cpp b/gpu-port/xkpi/xnu/nmx_fb.cpp
index 6a08779..ba1ca69 100644
--- a/gpu-port/xkpi/xnu/nmx_fb.cpp
+++ b/gpu-port/xkpi/xnu/nmx_fb.cpp
@@ -84,6 +84,16 @@ public:
     }
 
     bool start(IOService *provider) override {
+        /*
+         * IOFramebuffer::start finds this framebuffer's IOFBController by the IOFBDependentID property (one controller
+         * per GPU; IOFBController::copyController returns NULL without it). With no controller every later IOGraphics
+         * call that takes the controller's gate dereferences NULL+0x120: the first power change after
+         * registerPowerDriver panicked in IOFramebuffer::powerStateWillChangeTo (test 25). Set it as the GPU drivers
+         * do, to the PCI device's registry ID, with this framebuffer's index on it.
+         */
+        IOService *pci = provider->getProvider() ? provider->getProvider() : provider;
+        setProperty("IOFBDependentID", pci->getRegistryEntryID(), 64);
+        setProperty("IOFBDependentIndex", 0ULL, 32);
         nmx_trace("publish: start: IOFramebuffer::start", 0);
         if (!IOFramebuffer::start(provider)) return false;
         nmx_trace("publish: start: vblank timer (flags)", fFlags);
